cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code or its vehicle database, please cite the IAC 2026
  paper given under preferred-citation.
title: "Titan-mobility-system: preliminary sizing of a screw-propelled planetary rover"
type: software
abstract: >-
  A Phase 0/A sizing method for screw-propelled planetary rovers, with Titan
  as the reference case. A subsystem mass and power budget is coupled with a
  reduced-order screw-terrain model inside an iterative mass-closure loop,
  supported by a vehicle database in which every value carries its
  definition, evidence level and source. The screw-terrain block and the
  closure loop are validated against the full-scale trafficability tests of
  the Marsh Screw Amphibian. The code reproduces every table and figure of
  the paper.
